<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
    <dict>
        <key>Description</key>
        <string>Hands the downloaded WizTree installer (an .exe) to CimianImporter, which publishes it as a new version of the item into a Cimian repository (as a copy of the item's newest pkginfo, with what belongs to the installer file replaced), or says that nothing is new. The version label is the one that the download recipe's processor took from the installer's file name (4_33 gives 4.33), as written; CimianImporter does not read a version from an .exe. This is a dry run, which writes nothing, until the recipe's override sets cimian_dry_run to false. This recipe has not been run by anyone yet. The repository is the input cimian_repo or the AutoPkg preference CIMIAN_REPO. WizTree is free for personal use only: whether an organisation needs the vendor's licence is a question to settle before the item goes into a manifest.</string>
        <key>Identifier</key>
        <string>com.github.serrc-techops.cimian.WizTree</string>
        <key>Input</key>
        <dict>
            <key>CIMIAN_NAME</key>
            <string>wiztree</string>
            <key>CIMIAN_SUBDIRECTORY</key>
            <string></string>
            <key>NAME</key>
            <string>WizTree</string>
            <key>pkginfo</key>
            <dict>
                <key>developer</key>
                <string>Antibody Software</string>
                <key>display_name</key>
                <string>WizTree</string>
            </dict>
        </dict>
        <key>MinimumVersion</key>
        <string>1.0.0</string>
        <key>ParentRecipe</key>
        <string>com.github.serrc-techops.download.WizTree-Win</string>
        <key>Process</key>
        <array>
            <dict>
                <key>Processor</key>
                <string>com.github.serrc-techops.SharedProcessors/CimianImporter</string>
                <key>Arguments</key>
                <dict>
                    <key>pathname</key>
                    <string>%pathname%</string>
                    <key>cimian_name</key>
                    <string>%CIMIAN_NAME%</string>
                    <key>cimian_subdirectory</key>
                    <string>%CIMIAN_SUBDIRECTORY%</string>
                    <key>version</key>
                    <string>%version%</string>
                </dict>
            </dict>
        </array>
    </dict>
</plist>
